# Acquired full texts never enter version control: licence status varies per source and
# committing them is not reversible. Only hashes and metadata are tracked.
store/
*.pdf
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env

# Project instances may encode a consuming system's internal design. Only the worked
# example ships; real instances are kept out of a public repository deliberately.
projects/*
!projects/example-news-and-returns/
# The pilot corpus ships too, manifest and all. It exists because alembic-s4 stands below its floor and
# produces no verdicts, so the vertical slice needs a corpus built from public literature — which is what
# the privacy rule prescribes when a fresh instance is needed for a test. Its reading list is derived from
# its own discovery ledger by `tools/build_pilot_manifest.py`, so publishing it discloses nothing but
# public literature and the rule that selected it.
!projects/pilot-screen-time/
claimstone.egg-info/

# A project's curated source list is its reading list: same reason as projects/*. The pilot's is exempt
# above, because being readable is the point of it.
projects/*/manifest.tsv
!projects/pilot-screen-time/manifest.tsv
